## 12. Traditional Programming vs Artificial Intelligence

| Traditional Programming | AI / Machine Learning |
|---|---|
| Programmer writes explicit rules | Model learns patterns from examples |
| Logic is manually specified | Model parameters are learned during training |
| Best for clearly defined procedures | Useful for complex pattern-based tasks |
| Behaviour changes when code changes | Behaviour can change through retraining or configuration |
| Example: Calculator | Example: Spam classifier |

### Traditional Programming

```text
Input + Programmer-written Rules
              |
              v
            Output
```

### Machine Learning

```text
Training Data + Learning Algorithm
              |
              v
         Trained Model

New Input + Trained Model
              |
              v
            Output
```

