## 15. Case Study: AI-Based Spam Detection System

Consider an email service that automatically identifies spam messages.

### Problem

Users receive thousands of emails, and manually identifying spam is time-consuming.

### AI Solution

A machine-learning model can learn patterns from previously labelled emails.

### Working Process

```text
      Email Received
             |
             v
       Email Processing
             |
             v
      Feature Extraction
             |
             v
       Trained AI Model
             |
             v
      Classification
          /     \
         /       \
        v         v
      Spam    Not Spam
        |         |
        v         v
    Spam Folder  Inbox
```

### Example Features

- Number of suspicious links.
- Sender information.
- Presence of suspicious phrases.
- Email structure.
- Historical spam patterns.

### Benefits

- Reduces manual email filtering.
- Processes large volumes of emails.
- Helps identify suspicious messages.
- Can be improved using new labelled examples.

### Limitations

- Some legitimate emails may be marked as spam.
- Some spam emails may reach the inbox.
- Attackers may change their methods to avoid detection.

This demonstrates how AI can solve a practical problem while still requiring evaluation and improvement.

